    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="1189" n="1155" xml:id="pg1155"/>

                <head>588. Telegram From the Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        Venezuela<anchor n="1" xml:id="d588-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-06-07T19:56:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7,
                                1957—7:56 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>606. Your evaluation possible repercussions in Venezuela of restrictions on crude
                    oil imports your 658<anchor n="2" xml:id="d588-f2"/> appreciated. If possible
                    you and Venezuelan Embassy will be given advance notice any action this matter
                    and we will continue keep you fully informed developments.</p>
                <p>Difficult at present determine most opportune time proposed Chamber Commerce
                    delegation visit view following (1) Presidential Committee to investigate
                    Section 7 action not yet appointed;<anchor n="3" xml:id="d588-f3"/> (2) ODM
                    Director Gordon Gray has not yet completed consultation individual US oil
                    importing companies in effort explore feasibility achieving reduction imports by
                    voluntary action as directed by President. On balance however believe visit now
                    by Chamber delegation or other US group might be effective in presenting views
                    of US interests in Venezuela to press business and legislative circles during
                    important formative stage.</p>
                <p>Do not believe it necessary you visit US present time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d588-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d588-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 411.316/6–757. Confidential. Drafted
                    by Bartch and initialed by Rubottom.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d588-f2" n="2" xml:id="d588-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d387"><hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d588-f3" n="3" xml:id="d588-f3-content">
                <p>On June 26, the President announced the formation of the Special Committee to
                    Investigate Crude Oil Imports, composed of the Secretaries of State, Defense,
                    the Treasury, Commerce, Interior, and Labor.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
